  "id": "COMPOUND:18132 - PROTEIN:5866",
  "verbalization": "Lancifodilactone N appears to share a common mechanism of action with 5-Oxobrucine, which in turn targets NCI-H446. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which involve Lancifodilactone N acting as a target for 5-Oxobrucine, which then exerts its effects on NCI-H446. The evidence suggests that Lancifodilactone N may interact with Caspase-5 or Microtubule-associated protein 1B, both of which are targets of 5-Oxobrucine, and that this interaction leads to a downstream effect on NCI-H446. The consistent involvement of 5-Oxobrucine as a mediator across different pathways strengthens the hypothesis that Lancifodilactone N and NCI-H446 are linked through a shared target, likely via a pathway involving caspase activation or microtubule dynamics. The integration of these findings highlights a potential role for Lancifodilactone N in modulating cellular processes that ultimately influence NCI-H446.",
